stages.prompt_template:
A task just entered the Todo queue and needs a worker:

Title: {task_title}
Task ID: {task_id}
Priority: {task_priority}
Description: {task_description}
Acceptance criteria: {task_criteria}

Steps:
1. Call list_tasks(status_filter='in_progress') to check current workload.
2. If the task is already in_progress (another agent claimed it), stop — do nothing.
3. If you have capacity under your max_workers limit, call create_session(task_id='{task_id}') to spawn a worker. The worker will automatically mark the task in_progress and update status when done.
4. If at max capacity, call update_task(task_id='{task_id}', status='backlog', result_summary='Queue full — requeued to backlog') to hold it until a slot opens.
